  "summary": "DIR-086 complete - all four defects fixed, each confirmed with file:line evidence. S1 THE USER-VISIBLE BUG (Quick-Pitch routing): CandidateExecutiveRail.jsx:106 resolved an action's destination as action.routes[0], and in copilotActions.js all three candidate actions listed /dashboard FIRST - candidate-tailor-resume routes ['/dashboard','/build-resume'] at :55, candidate-cover-letter routes ['/dashboard','/cover-letter'] at :65, candidate-mock-interview routes ['/dashboard','/dashboard/interview'] at :75 - so every Quick-Pitch click navigated to the page the user was already on. candidate-mock-interview already carried the correct navigateTo at :84 but the rail never read it, and /cover-letter at :65 is not a mounted route at all. FIX: each candidate action now carries an explicit navigateTo (/build-resume/heading, /dashboard/cover-letters, /dashboard/interview) and its routes array was reordered so /dashboard is never first; a new exported resolveActionHref(action) in copilotActions.js is the single resolver - navigateTo wins when present, otherwise the MOST SPECIFIC (longest) route is chosen rather than routes[0] - and the rail now calls that resolver. S2 ZERO AWKWARD HORIZONTAL SCROLLBARS: the pill row at DashboardHomepage.jsx:1179 was plain overflow-x-auto with no scrollbar styling, so the browser painted its native track. SECOND-ORDER BUG FOUND: the class the repo already used for this, scrollbar-none at EducationStep.jsx:469 and WorkHistoryStep.jsx:285, is a NO-OP because package.json pins tailwindcss ^4.1.8 with NO scrollbar plugin installed, so it generates no CSS at all. FIX: all three rows now use the Tailwind v4 arbitrary utilities [scrollbar-width:none] and [&::-webkit-scrollbar]:hidden, which need no plugin, and stay scrollable and keyboard reachable. S3 STREAMLINED CARD: the card rendered a primary button at :1552 then a 2x2 grid of four full-width secondary buttons spanning :1566-1650, producing the stacked wall and excess height. FIX: the action area is now a wrapping row - the primary Edit Resume action claims its own full row (flex-1 basis-full) and the PDF, Word and Share actions share ONE compact row (flex-1 min-w-0) - so the card is two rows instead of four, with the existing overflow menu at :1460-1490 and the premium gating untouched. S4 STREAMLINED RAIL: CandidateExecutiveRail rendered three widgets and the ATS Keyword Strength (:129) and Application Milestones (:153) ones repeated exactly what the DIR-085 metric capsule strip already shows, which is why the rail overflowed. FIX: both duplicated widgets were deleted so the rail holds ONLY the Live Copilot Quick-Pitch and fits the viewport, and their data reads (getResumes/getTrackedJobs/getStatesOfUser) plus the 4s retry interval went with them, which also drops three API calls from the Overview first paint; the Quick-Pitch empty state is kept. S5 TESTS: new tests/dir086-candidate-overview-polish.test.mjs with 6 acceptance tests (AC1 every candidate Quick-Pitch resolves to its real destination and never to /dashboard, AC2 the resolver prefers navigateTo and otherwise the most specific route and the rail no longer indexes routes[0], AC3 the pill row hides its track with the real utilities and the repo no longer relies on the no-op scrollbar-none anywhere, AC4 the rail renders exactly one widget and the orphaned reads and retry loop are gone, AC5 the card is one primary action plus a compact wrapping row with the overflow menu intact, AC6 a11y and the dependency budget) and test:dir086 registered; two superseded pins updated in lockstep (DIR-077 three-widget rail and DIR-085 two-widget rail). VERIFIED: dir086 6 passing, 161 passing across dir086 + dir085 + dir084 + dir083 + dir082 + dir081 + dir080 + dir079 + dir078 + dir077 + dir048 suites + dir055 + cuba-candidate-portal + cuba-design-system + copilot-command-surface, test:dir072..dir086 and test:design-system every script EXIT 0, test:product EXIT 0 on a quiet run, security:static 67 passing, xampp-policy 4 passing, build EXIT 0 in 2.77s measured with no concurrent load against a 4.0s budget, lint 0 errors, frozen cv-templates diff 0. MEASUREMENT NOTE: an earlier build reading of 4.94s was taken immediately after the full product suite finished on the same machine; quiet, the build is 2.77s. HONEST LIMITS: the Share action still appears in the card's compact row as well as in the overflow menu, because removing the standalone button would have changed the premium gating path, so only its height was reduced; the scrollbar fix changes what the user sees rather than what the browser does, since the rows remain scrollable and simply no longer paint a track; and the rail showing fewer widgets is the requested de-duplication rather than a loss of data, since the same ATS and application figures remain on the page in the metric capsule strip. The wider DIR-082 legacy backlog is unchanged and still ratcheted. ZERO FABRICATION: no metric was invented or hidden, every Quick-Pitch destination is a real mounted route asserted by AC1, and the rail's remaining action list comes from the platform's own getCopilotActions."
